latticelink3dnl_assembly.out
Assembly check for the geometrically nonlinear lattice: nl shell (lattice3dnl) + nl bonds (latticelink3dnl) + nl rebar, in the single-strut RC bending config (cf. jobs .../Single). Exercises the bond spin_B route (rebar node rotates) and the nl hybrid shell, which the isolated latticelink3dnl_rotation test does not. At these small rotations the response must match the corresponding linear-element model.
NonLinearStatic nmsteps 1 nsteps 15 contextOutputStep 1000 nmodules 1
nsteps 15 rtolf 1.e-3 maxiter 300 stiffMode 1 controllmode 1 refloadmode 1 minsteplength 1.e-3
errorcheck
domain 3dLattice
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 4 nelem 4 ncrosssect 3 nmat 3 nbc 2 nic 0 nltf 2
node 1 coords 3 0.0 0.0 0.0 bc 6 1 1 1 1 1 1
node 2 coords 3 5.0e-2 0.0 0.0 bc 6 0 1 0 1 2 1
node 3 coords 3 0.0 0.0 -1.1e-2
node 4 coords 3 5.0e-2 0.0 -1.1e-2
lattice3dnl 1 nodes 2 1 2 crossSect 1 mat 1 shellnormal 3 0.0 0.0 1.0 polycoords 12 0.025 0.02 0.022   0.025 -0.02 0.022   0.025 -0.02 -0.022   0.025 0.02 -0.022
lattice3Dnl 2 nodes 2 3 4 crossSect 2 mat 2
latticelink3Dnl 3 nodes 2 1 3 crossSect 3 mat 3 length 2.5e-2 diameter 5.2e-3 dirvector 3 1.0 0.0 0.0
latticelink3Dnl 4 nodes 2 2 4 crossSect 3 mat 3 length 2.5e-2 diameter 5.2e-3 dirvector 3 1.0 0.0 0.0
LatticeCS 1 material 1 shape 2 nlayers 8
LatticeCS 2 material 2 shape 1 radius 0.0026
LatticeCS 3 material 3 shape 1 radius 0.0026
LatticeDamageShell 1 d 2400. talpha 0.0 em 28.6e9 nu 0.15 e0 70.e-6 wf 1.5e-5 stype 3 coh 2. ec 30
LatticeFrameSteelPlastic 2 d 7850. talpha 0.0 e 200.e9 n 0.0 sigmay 350.e6 htype 1 h_eps 3 0. 0.003 1.e9 h(eps) 3 1.0 1. 1.
LatticeSlip 3 d 1. talpha 0.0 e 200.e9 a1 100. a2 100. t0 4.e6 type 1 s1 1.e-5 alpha 0.5
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 prescribedvalue 0.0
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 2 prescribedvalue -1.5e-2
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1.0
PiecewiseLinFunction 2 nPoints 2 t 2 0. 15. f(t) 2 0. 1.
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-2
## Reaction moment at node 2 dof 5 (prescribed rotation): nl shell + nl bonds + nl rebar.
## tStep N is at theta_y = -1e-3*(N-1) (step 1 is the theta=0 state). The response rises to a
## cracking peak, softens, then climbs as the steel takes over; it must stay ~ the linear-element
## model at these small rotations.
#REACTION tStep 8  number 2 dof 5 value -5.3328e+01
#REACTION tStep 15 number 2 dof 5 value -5.6011e+01
#%END_CHECK%
